cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mixdra: Mixture Dose-Response Analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it implements."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sam
    family-names: van Loon
    affiliation: "Amsterdam Institute for Life and Environment (A-LIFE), Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"
  - given-names: Jelle
    family-names: Kalsbeek
  - given-names: Ge
    family-names: Xie
    affiliation: "Institute for Biodiversity and Ecosystem Dynamics, University of Amsterdam"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SvL-1/mixdra"
abstract: >-
  An R package implementing the Jonker et al. (2005) mixture dose-response
  methodology. Fits single-chemical and binary/ternary mixture models using the
  concentration addition and independent action reference models, quantifies
  synergistic/antagonistic, dose-ratio-dependent and dose-level-dependent
  deviations from additivity, and selects the supported interaction pattern by
  likelihood-ratio testing. Ships with a Shiny dashboard for non-programmers.
keywords:
  - mixture toxicity
  - dose-response
  - ecotoxicology
  - concentration addition
  - independent action
  - R
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
